  {
    "id": "2c5333de8b5c9e760296",
    "source": "A line that follows with [Card played: ...] is the structured action the player chose from their hand: resolve exactly that with the tool it names. A card line's parenthesised arguments are the tool's own: pass them as written (bonus=true to take_action, bonusAttack, stunningStrike, reckless or nonlethal to pc_attack, variant to use_resource, trigger to take_action ready). A player may play a reaction card on another character's turn (Shield, Uncanny Dodge, Cutting Words...): its line names the reaction, and you resolve it with use_reaction at once, even though it is not their turn, and it is not their turn's action.",
